  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404554",
      "title": "Accessing Protected Resources",
      "lectureOrder": 184,
      "videoOrder": 180,
      "sourceHash": "9e7ce2a25c07089dee8bc0b0b4a4254467615e4f39a930699acb7199d04b443e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "Now, what can we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 6.95,
          "en": "with this token that we manage now, our context?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.95,
          "end": 8.83,
          "en": "At the moment, we're only using it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.83,
          "end": 12.68,
          "en": "to find out whether a user is authenticated or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.68,
          "end": 16.04,
          "en": "And that is one of the main use cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.04,
          "end": 18.73,
          "en": "or at least it's a very important use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.73,
          "end": 21.73,
          "en": "but the token also plays another role.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.73,
          "end": 23.45,
          "en": "This token is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.45,
          "end": 26.56,
          "en": "by our Firebase project here so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.56,
          "end": 28.66,
          "en": "And we can also use this token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.66,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "to get access to protected resources we might have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 34,
          "en": "on our backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34,
          "end": 37.25,
          "en": "Now, at the moment, we have no protected resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.25,
          "end": 39.42,
          "en": "but we can change this now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.42,
          "end": 41.71,
          "en": "For that, let's go to the Realtime Database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.71,
          "end": 45.24,
          "en": "and let's add a new node there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.24,
          "end": 47.14,
          "en": "You can also delete the expenses node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.14,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "if you still have that from earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 51.73,
          "en": "or you can keep it, it doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.73,
          "end": 53.409,
          "en": "We're not going to use it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.409,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "But we will create a new node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 58.16,
          "en": "by adding a child here in our database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.16,
          "end": 60.32,
          "en": "and I will name this node message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.27,
          "end": 64.52,
          "en": "and enter Hello World here as a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.52,
          "end": 65.633,
          "en": "between double quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.73,
          "end": 69.94,
          "en": "So now I entered this extra data into my database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.94,
          "end": 72.96000000000001,
          "en": "and this is now not a node with nested data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 74.42,
          "en": "but instead, it is a node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.42,
          "end": 77.023,
          "en": "that directly holds a string as data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.2,
          "end": 80.3,
          "en": "Now, I wanna fetch that string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.3,
          "end": 81.96000000000001,
          "en": "from inside my WelcomeScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.96000000000001,
          "end": 83.97,
          "en": "simply as a demo, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 88.713,
          "en": "That's not super useful functionality but it is a nice demo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 90.86,
          "en": "In order to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 90.86,
          "end": 95.59,
          "en": "we can send a HTTP request in the WelcomeScreen to Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.59,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "to get that node here, to get that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now, we could create a utility helper file for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 106.21000000000001,
          "en": "but to keep things simple, I'll send that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.21000000000001,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "from directly inside this component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 112.493,
          "en": "by using axios inside of the WelcomeScreen component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "Then we can add the useEffect hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 117.47,
          "en": "to execute an effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.47,
          "end": 120.76,
          "en": "right when the component is first loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.76,
          "end": 123.17,
          "en": "so that we send the request when the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.17,
          "end": 124.31,
          "en": "is first loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.31,
          "end": 127.25,
          "en": "And in here, we can then send a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.25,
          "end": 130.4,
          "en": "to that node, so to that database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.4,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "and then that node we set up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 134.89,
          "en": "For that, you can click on message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.89,
          "end": 137.44,
          "en": "and then grab this URL here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 139.07999999999998,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "and that's the URL we wanna send the request to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 143.32,
          "en": "though here on Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.32,
          "end": 146.083,
          "en": "we also have to add .json at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.75,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "This will now send a get request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 154.273,
          "en": "And then I wanna use that data to output it here as text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.24,
          "end": 157.7,
          "en": "For that, we can manage some state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.7,
          "end": 159.323,
          "en": "in the WelcomeScreen component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.96,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "And get our fetchedMessage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 166.483,
          "en": "and update it with setFetchedMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 170.29,
          "en": "And initially, that's an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 171.46,
          "end": 172.31,
          "en": "But then here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.31,
          "end": 175.34300000000002,
          "en": "I wanna update this once I got back my message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 176.3,
          "end": 178.07999999999998,
          "en": "Now, for this we could use async await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 180.4,
          "en": "and wrap this into a extra function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.4,
          "end": 182.82,
          "en": "because this function, this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 186.33,
          "en": "should not be turned into an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 186.33,
          "end": 189.26,
          "en": "or we use promises in the good old way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 189.26,
          "end": 190.459,
          "en": "by adding then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.459,
          "end": 195.12,
          "en": "and then here, we get our response in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.12,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "which we pass to the then block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 200.02,
          "en": "and in this response, we will have a data object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 200.02,
          "end": 201.67000000000002,
          "en": "which should hold our message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201.67000000000002,
          "end": 204.15,
          "en": "or which should be our message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 204.15,
          "end": 205.66,
          "en": "So to see whether that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 205.66,
          "end": 209.99,
          "en": "let's simply quickly console.log response.data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.99,
          "end": 213.09,
          "en": "and not do anything with the state for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 213.09,
          "end": 215.63,
          "en": "And if we do this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 215.63,
          "end": 220.39,
          "en": "and we reload, and we then log in again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.39,
          "end": 222.55,
          "en": "we should see something here in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 222.55,
          "end": 224.603,
          "en": "and indeed, we see Hello World here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 225.73,
          "end": 228.5,
          "en": "So therefore now, we can then call setFetchedMessage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 228.5,
          "end": 231.14,
          "en": "and set this equal to response.data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 231.14,
          "end": 233.68,
          "en": "So equal to that text we're fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 233.68,
          "end": 235.36,
          "en": "and then here in this text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 235.36,
          "end": 237.613,
          "en": "we can output fetchedMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 238.78,
          "end": 241.31,
          "en": "If we do all of that and we reload again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 241.31,
          "end": 244.62,
          "en": "what you will see is that it crashed on Android",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 244.62,
          "end": 246.58,
          "en": "but we can ignore this for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 246.58,
          "end": 248.62,
          "en": "If I test this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 248.62,
          "end": 250.33,
          "en": "we get Hello World!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 250.33,
          "end": 253.62,
          "en": "And it loads a little bit after the rest of this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 253.62,
          "end": 255.55,
          "en": "because it has to be fetched first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 255.55,
          "end": 259.11,
          "en": "but ultimately, Hello World arrives here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 259.11,
          "end": 261.62,
          "en": "And of course, this would also work on Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 261.62,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "If we give this a try here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 267.963,
          "en": "and we enter our details there, it also loads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 269.23,
          "end": 271.2,
          "en": "So that's loading this text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 271.2,
          "end": 273.07,
          "en": "but why am I showing this to you?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.07,
          "end": 275.53,
          "en": "There is nothing new about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 275.53,
          "end": 278.71,
          "en": "Well, indeed there is nothing new about this yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 278.71,
          "end": 280.54,
          "en": "At the moment, we can send this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 280.54,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "and get this data just like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 282.72,
          "end": 287.693,
          "en": "because this API, this Database API is not protected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 288.82,
          "end": 291.15,
          "en": "If you have a look at the rules here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 291.15,
          "end": 293.9,
          "en": "where you can control the protection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 293.9,
          "end": 295.69,
          "en": "in the end, we have no rules here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 295.69,
          "end": 298.31,
          "en": "that would lock down this database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 298.31,
          "end": 300.15,
          "en": "Even if you don't fully understand this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 300.15,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "I can tell you that this grants us access to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 306.8,
          "en": "or to the API to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 306.8,
          "end": 309.11,
          "en": "And if you would be building your own API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 309.11,
          "end": 311.64,
          "en": "you also might have URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 311.64,
          "end": 313.773,
          "en": "that are accessible to everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 314.66,
          "end": 317.48,
          "en": "But you also might wanna have certain routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 317.48,
          "end": 320.72,
          "en": "certain endpoints that are only accessible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 320.72,
          "end": 323.11,
          "en": "by authenticated users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 323.11,
          "end": 325.01,
          "en": "Now, we do log our users in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 325.01,
          "end": 326.86,
          "en": "but at the moment here on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 326.86,
          "end": 328.1,
          "en": "there is no connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 328.1,
          "end": 331.913,
          "en": "between a user being authenticated and our data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 332.9,
          "end": 335.911,
          "en": "Because backend APIs like this are stateless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 335.911,
          "end": 339.34000000000003,
          "en": "Firebase doesn't store the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 339.34000000000003,
          "end": 341.46,
          "en": "that a user did log in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 341.46,
          "end": 343.563,
          "en": "That's why we are getting this token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 347.08,
          "en": "We can use this token to grant access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 347.08,
          "end": 350.5,
          "en": "or to get access to protected endpoints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 350.5,
          "end": 352.96,
          "en": "For that we need to protect endpoints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 352.96,
          "end": 354.53,
          "en": "as a first step though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 354.53,
          "end": 356.26,
          "en": "And here on Firebase, we can do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 356.26,
          "end": 359.94,
          "en": "by changing those rules, for example, for reading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 359.94,
          "end": 361.84,
          "en": "Here you could add a rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 361.84,
          "end": 366.84,
          "en": "where you say auth.uid is not equal to null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 367.2,
          "end": 369.98,
          "en": "This means that now read requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 369.98,
          "end": 373.72,
          "en": "are only allowed if we do have a valid user ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 373.72,
          "end": 376.39,
          "en": "so if a user is authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 376.39,
          "end": 378.84,
          "en": "if the incoming request can prove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 378.84,
          "end": 381.52,
          "en": "that a user is authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 381.52,
          "end": 386.01,
          "en": "And that uid will be part of that token, which we get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 386.01,
          "end": 387.78,
          "en": "We can do the same here for writing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 387.78,
          "end": 389.59,
          "en": "and also lock this down.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 389.59,
          "end": 392.33,
          "en": "If we now publish those rules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 392.33,
          "end": 394.24,
          "en": "we won't be able to fetch our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 394.24,
          "end": 397.52,
          "en": "without proving that we are authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 397.52,
          "end": 399.553,
          "en": "So now if we reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 401.56,
          "end": 404.15,
          "en": "and we quickly try this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 404.15,
          "end": 407.03,
          "en": "we can log in but now Hello World",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 407.03,
          "end": 409.82,
          "en": "is not showing up because this request fails",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 409.82,
          "end": 411.76,
          "en": "as we can also tell by this warning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 411.76,
          "end": 414.373,
          "en": "which tells us that some error wasn't handled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 415.72,
          "end": 418.40999999999997,
          "en": "And that's the problem we can now also solve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 418.40999999999997,
          "end": 421.74,
          "en": "with this token because if we attach the token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 421.74,
          "end": 423.17,
          "en": "to this outgoing request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 423.17,
          "end": 426.62,
          "en": "we can prove to Firebase that we are authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 426.62,
          "end": 429.15,
          "en": "Firebase will then have a look at the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 429.15,
          "end": 430.64,
          "en": "validate the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 430.64,
          "end": 432.98,
          "en": "and extract information like the user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 432.98,
          "end": 435.86,
          "en": "from the token and then grant us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 435.86,
          "end": 437.6,
          "en": "if the token is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 437.6,
          "end": 439.96,
          "en": "If it's not, we don't get access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 439.96,
          "end": 441.33,
          "en": "And how can this be achieved?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 441.33,
          "end": 443.55,
          "en": "How can we add the token here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 443.55,
          "end": 445.287,
          "en": "Well, in Firebase case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 445.287,
          "end": 449.34,
          "en": "we simply have to add the auth query parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 449.34,
          "end": 451.18,
          "en": "to the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 451.18,
          "end": 453.1,
          "en": "For other APIs, it might be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 453.1,
          "end": 454.67,
          "en": "You might need to add a header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 454.67,
          "end": 457.47,
          "en": "but here we just add the auth query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 457.47,
          "end": 460.61,
          "en": "and set this equal to our token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 460.61,
          "end": 462.72,
          "en": "Therefore, we need to get our token here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 462.72,
          "end": 464.727,
          "en": "with useContext and AuthContext,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 466.52,
          "end": 468.83,
          "en": "so we have to import these things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 468.83,
          "end": 472.3,
          "en": "We have to get this data here in the WelcomeScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 472.3,
          "end": 474.523,
          "en": "and then we can use our token here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 475.4,
          "end": 479.78,
          "en": "We can get our token by accessing authCtx.token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 483.15,
          "end": 485.55,
          "en": "Add it as a dependency here on useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 485.55,
          "end": 487.83,
          "en": "because we're going to use it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 487.83,
          "end": 491.18,
          "en": "Here we're going to add it at the end of the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 491.18,
          "end": 494.8,
          "en": "by simply adding it to it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 494.8,
          "end": 498.08,
          "en": "Now the token is added to the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 498.08,
          "end": 502,
          "en": "with that query parameter, this auth query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 502,
          "end": 505.32,
          "en": "and that token therefore is sent to Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 505.32,
          "end": 508.7,
          "en": "and that token will then prove that we are authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 508.7,
          "end": 510.87,
          "en": "If it's valid, which this token will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 510.87,
          "end": 512,
          "en": "since we are storing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 512,
          "end": 514.433,
          "en": "and using the token provided by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 515.42,
          "end": 519.41,
          "en": "If we now save this and reload, and we try this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 519.41,
          "end": 521.603,
          "en": "here if we log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 523.26,
          "end": 524.32,
          "en": "I got an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 524.32,
          "end": 526.65,
          "en": "because this is not AuthContext,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 526.65,
          "end": 530.47,
          "en": "this should be AuthContext, not AuthContent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 530.47,
          "end": 531.76,
          "en": "AuthContent is a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 531.76,
          "end": 533.97,
          "en": "This should be AuthContext.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 533.97,
          "end": 536.88,
          "en": "So now we should be able to tab into the context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 536.88,
          "end": 539.01,
          "en": "But now with that if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 539.01,
          "end": 540.883,
          "en": "and we try to log in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 542.4,
          "end": 544.04,
          "en": "this works, and now Hello World",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 544.04,
          "end": 545.75,
          "en": "is fetched successfully again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 545.75,
          "end": 548.26,
          "en": "because now we're sending along that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 548.26,
          "end": 550.97,
          "en": "that proves that we are authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 550.97,
          "end": 554.35,
          "en": "And that's another important role that token plays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 554.35,
          "end": 555.94,
          "en": "It's not just used in our app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 555.94,
          "end": 558.94,
          "en": "to find out whether a user did log in or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 558.94,
          "end": 560.47,
          "en": "it is important for that as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 560.47,
          "end": 562.09,
          "en": "but it's not just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 562.09,
          "end": 564.68,
          "en": "Instead, it's also used on a API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 564.68,
          "end": 567.44,
          "en": "to find out if a request is coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 567.44,
          "end": 570.3,
          "en": "from an authenticated user or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 570.3,
          "end": 574.68,
          "en": "because typically, REST APIs don't store that information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 574.68,
          "end": 578.01,
          "en": "They don't know if any random app's user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 578.01,
          "end": 580.29,
          "en": "is authenticated or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 580.29,
          "end": 582.26,
          "en": "Instead, you have to send the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 582.26,
          "end": 583.83,
          "en": "that you are authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 583.83,
          "end": 586.72,
          "en": "that token along with the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 586.72,
          "end": 590.09,
          "en": "that is targeting a protected resource.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 590.09,
          "end": 592.89,
          "en": "Like our API here, which is protected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 592.89,
          "end": 594.9,
          "en": "because of these rules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 594.9,
          "end": 597.69,
          "en": "Now, these rules are Firebase specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 597.69,
          "end": 601.38,
          "en": "but the general idea is the same for all APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 601.38,
          "end": 604.09,
          "en": "The token is your ticket to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 604.09,
          "end": 606.89,
          "en": "and that's why we are managing it on the front end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 606.89,
          "end": 609.1,
          "en": "and why we don't just use it to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 609.1,
          "end": 611.16,
          "en": "whether a user is authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 611.16,
          "end": 615.003,
          "en": "but why we also attach it to outgoing HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
